{
 "_comment": "CAD profiles of the Gerber import: markers that identify the program that wrote a set of files, and the layer-name rules of each program. Markers: scope gerber, drill, support (any other text file), name (file name), odb (ODB++ misc/info); weight 9 or more is decisive (the file names its generator or carries a quirk only that tool writes), 4 to 8 a quirk or convention, 1 to 3 shared. status: R = seen in a real sample file, D = a documented statement, M = from memory, not seen. name_rules_status M = names from memory (PADS, EAGLE). Only tools with real samples have a profile; there is none for Zuken, CADSTAR, PADS Professional, Xpedition VX, Allegro X, OrCAD X, EasyEDA Pro or Horizon. Every pattern is bounded so that its worst case on a head of 8 kB is linear. No profile presets the bottom-side X sign of a placement file (it is detected from the paste openings).",
